From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:09:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/35] H18: catch image-codec panics at the codec boundary

Run each call into an image codec crate (zune-jpeg, hayro-ccitt,
hayro-jbig2, hayro-jpeg2000) inside catch_unwind through one helper,
guard_codec, and turn a panic into DecodeFailure::ImageDecode, so a codec
bug skips one image instead of failing the page. Only the codec calls are
guarded: image parameters, JBIG2Globals resolution and the rest of the
parser still panic.

The catch is compiled out under cfg(fuzzing) (set by cargo fuzz) and
without std, so fuzzing still sees every codec panic; the manifest
declares the cfg. The test-only feature codec-panic-hook adds
arm_codec_panic_for_test (panic inside the guard on the next codec call)
and arm_unguarded_image_panic_for_test (panic in the codec module, after
parameter resolution, just before the guard), both per thread and cleared when they fire.

Refs internal #76
